[SECTION]
TITLE: Context

[TEXT]
Feature: **FACADE-SPLIT** — Cleave OS-touching addons out of the
``String_Types`` facade into Ada child packages, so the strings layer
stays focused and SPARK-clean.

Today ``String_Types`` is a god-package: it re-exports the command-line
bridge (``Argument_Count``, ``Argument``, ``Set_Exit_Status``, …), the
environment-variable bridge, the ``Ada.Directories`` bridge and the
``Ada.Text_IO``-style bridge alongside the strings API. Consumers that
need only string operations are still forced to compile against
``Ada.Command_Line`` transitively, which (a) muddies the SPARK story —
``Anystrings`` is ``SPARK_Mode On`` but the addons are ``SPARK_Mode
Off`` — and (b) drags OS-coupling into every translation unit that says
``with String_Types;``.

This document covers **Layer 1** of a two-layer plan. Layer 1 splits the
*facade* — i.e. it moves the user-visible ``renames`` for the
command-line bridge out of ``String_Types`` and into the Ada child
package ``String_Types.Command_Line``. Layer 2 (out of scope here)
extracts the environment / directories / Text_IO bridges from the
``Anystrings`` generic formals into standalone per-backend packages,
so that a similar child-package split can be applied to them while
also satisfying the dependency-isolation invariant
(FUNC-FACADE-004).

The decision to keep environment / directories / Text_IO inside
``String_Types`` for Layer 1 is deliberate. Those three bridges are
declared as **generic formal parameters** of the ``Anystrings`` package
(``src/anystrings.ads``) and are instantiated via the per-backend
``<X>_String_Operations`` package, whose spec ``with``s
``Ada.Text_IO`` publicly. Moving only the *renames* into child
packages while leaving the generic structure unchanged would not
isolate the OS-unit dependency closure: every consumer of
``String_Types`` would still pull ``Ada.Text_IO``,
``Ada.Environment_Variables`` and ``Ada.Directories`` through the
``with String_Types -> with <X>_Strings -> with
<X>_String_Operations`` chain. Achieving true isolation for those
three requires restructuring the generic, which is Layer 2.

The command-line bridge, by contrast, is already a hand-rolled
per-backend package (``<X>_Command_Line``) that is **not** declared
as a formal of the ``Anystrings`` generic. Its facade can therefore
be split into a child package today with a clean dependency-isolation
guarantee.

All five bundled backends (``standard``, ``wide_string``,
``wide_wide_string``, ``uxstring``, ``vss``) MUST expose an identical
public surface for the new child package, mirroring the parity rule
already established for ``String_Types`` itself (FUNC-CMDLINE-009).

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: Facade Shape

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FUNC-FACADE-001
STATUS: Approved
PRIORITY: Must
TITLE: String_Types is strings-only
STATEMENT: >>>
The package ``String_Types`` SHALL NOT re-export any subprogram, type,
constant, or subtype belonging to the command-line bridge feature
(FUNC-CMDLINE-001..009).

The strings-shaped surface — ``String_Type``, ``Character_Type``,
``Empty_String``, the comparison operators, conversion helpers
(``To_String_Type``, ``To_Latin_1``, ``To_UTF_8``, ``From_UTF_8`` and
their result types), the character-classification predicates, the
case-mapping subprograms, the substring-search and substitution
helpers, the prefix / suffix predicates, the Latin-1 lossy-detection
helpers, and the Hash function — SHALL remain accessible from
``String_Types`` directly.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
This is the facade-cleanup invariant. After this change, a consumer
that needs only string operations writes ``with String_Types;`` and
inherits no command-line surface. The environment / directories /
Text_IO surfaces remain on ``String_Types`` for now (see Context for
why); they are scheduled for Layer 2.
<<<
RELATIONS: FUNC-CMDLINE-009

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FUNC-FACADE-002
STATUS: Approved
PRIORITY: Must
TITLE: Command-line bridge exposed via String_Types.Command_Line child package
STATEMENT: >>>
The command-line bridge SHALL be exposed to user code as an Ada child
package of ``String_Types``, named ``String_Types.Command_Line``.

The child package SHALL re-export, by Ada ``renames`` or equivalent
mechanism, the entirety of the public surface introduced by
FUNC-CMDLINE-001..009:

- The argument-count function (FUNC-CMDLINE-001).
- The argument-access function (FUNC-CMDLINE-002, FUNC-CMDLINE-003).
- The command-name function (FUNC-CMDLINE-004).
- The exit-status subtype together with the ``Success`` and ``Failure``
  constants (FUNC-CMDLINE-005).
- Both ``Set_Exit_Status`` overloads (FUNC-CMDLINE-006, FUNC-CMDLINE-007).

The signatures of these declarations in ``String_Types.Command_Line``
SHALL be identical to those previously exposed by ``String_Types``;
only the package qualification at the call site changes.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
"Identical signature" means same name, same parameter profile, same
return type, same enumeration-literal visibility. Existing call sites
that previously wrote ``Argument_Count`` (relying on ``use
String_Types;``) will now write ``Argument_Count`` (relying on ``use
String_Types.Command_Line;`` in addition).

The right-hand side of each ``renames`` differs per backend
(``Standard_Command_Line``, ``Wide_Command_Line``, …); this is the
existing per-backend package that already exists in
``src/strings/<dir>/<X>_command_line.ads/adb`` and is unchanged by
this feature.
<<<
RELATIONS: FUNC-CMDLINE-001, FUNC-CMDLINE-002, FUNC-CMDLINE-003, FUNC-CMDLINE-004, FUNC-CMDLINE-005, FUNC-CMDLINE-006, FUNC-CMDLINE-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FUNC-FACADE-003
STATUS: Approved
PRIORITY: Must
TITLE: String_Types.Command_Line has identical surface across all five backends
STATEMENT: >>>
The package ``String_Types.Command_Line`` SHALL be present in every one
of the five bundled backend directories
(``src/strings/{standard,wide_string,wide_wide_string,uxstring,vss}/``)
and SHALL expose the same set of declarations with the same public
signatures across all five.

Only the right-hand side of each ``renames`` MAY differ between
backends (it MUST reference the local per-backend ``<X>_Command_Line``
implementation package).

User source code that ``with``s ``String_Types.Command_Line``,
optionally ``use``s it, and calls any of the declared subprograms
SHALL compile unchanged under any of the five backends.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
This is the generalisation of FUNC-CMDLINE-009 to the new child
package. The parity rule is the same property that already governs
the rest of ``String_Types``: backend swap MUST be a build-time
source-directory substitution with zero consumer-side change.

Mechanically: the left-hand-side declarations of all five copies of
``string_types-command_line.ads`` MUST be byte-identical to each other
up to (a) the ``with`` clause and (b) the right-hand side of each
``renames``. No backend MAY add or remove a subprogram from the child
package.
<<<
RELATIONS: FUNC-FACADE-002, FUNC-CMDLINE-009

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: Dependency Isolation

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FUNC-FACADE-004
STATUS: Approved
PRIORITY: Must
TITLE: Pure String_Types consumers do not pull Ada.Command_Line transitively
STATEMENT: >>>
A user compilation unit whose context clause is ``with String_Types;``
(without ``with String_Types.Command_Line;``) SHALL NOT have
``Ada.Command_Line`` in its semantic dependence closure.

Equivalently: the unit-list produced by ``gnatbind`` for a program
``with String_Types; procedure P is begin null; end P;`` SHALL NOT
contain a reference to ``Ada.Command_Line``.

This SHALL hold for all five bundled backends.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
This is the dependency-isolation invariant — the core observable gain
of Layer 1. Before the split, the closure
``String_Types -> <X>_Command_Line -> Ada.Command_Line`` was forced
on every user. After the split, ``Ada.Command_Line`` enters the
closure only when the user explicitly opts in by saying
``with String_Types.Command_Line;``.

Verification is performed at the build-system level rather than at
runtime: a build-time check in
``examples/run_all_backends_demo.sh`` (or an equivalent script)
inspects the generated ``.ali`` file for the isolation-test program
and asserts the absence of ``Ada.Command_Line`` in the unit list.

Note that this requirement scopes only the command-line bridge.
The analogous guarantee for ``Ada.Environment_Variables``,
``Ada.Directories`` and ``Ada.Text_IO`` is NOT in scope for Layer 1
because their implementations are wired through ``Anystrings``
generic formals; achieving isolation for them requires the Layer 2
generic-restructure.
<<<
RELATIONS: FUNC-FACADE-001, FUNC-FACADE-002

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: Internal Layout

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FUNC-FACADE-005
STATUS: Approved
PRIORITY: Should
TITLE: Per-backend implementation packages keep their existing flat names
STATEMENT: >>>
The existing per-backend implementation packages
``Standard_Command_Line``, ``Wide_Command_Line``,
``Wide_Wide_Command_Line``, ``UXString_Command_Line`` and
``VSS_Command_Line`` (one per backend, located at
``src/strings/<dir>/<prefix>_command_line.{ads,adb}``) SHALL retain
their current names and file paths.

These packages SHALL NOT be made Ada child packages of either
``Anystrings`` or ``String_Types``; they remain top-level
implementation units.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
The implementation packages are not user-visible — consumers go
through ``String_Types.Command_Line``. Renaming them to mirror the
new facade hierarchy (e.g. ``Anystrings.Command_Line.Standard``)
would churn the directory-swap mechanism, which relies on per-backend
flat source directories under ``src/strings/<dir>/``. The cost is
high and the benefit is internal-only.

The implementation packages MAY be relocated or restructured in a
future refactor (Layer 2 or later); this requirement only mandates
the *Layer 1* status quo.
<<<
RELATIONS: FUNC-FACADE-002

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: Future Work (Layer 2)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FUNC-FACADE-006
STATUS: Draft
PRIORITY: Could
TITLE: Layer 2 — extract Environment / Directories / Text_IO bridges from the Anystrings generic
STATEMENT: >>>
A future feature SHALL extract the environment, filesystem
(``Ada.Directories``) and Text_IO bridges out of the ``Anystrings``
generic formals into standalone per-backend implementation packages
(mirroring the existing ``<X>_Command_Line`` pattern). Once that is
done, the present facade-split treatment SHALL be applied to those
three surfaces, producing the additional child packages
``String_Types.Environment``, ``String_Types.Directories`` and
``String_Types.Text_IO`` and extending the FUNC-FACADE-004
dependency-isolation invariant to them.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
This is a forward-looking requirement, deliberately scoped to
``Could`` priority. It MAY be re-prioritised (or split into three
separate requirements, one per addon) once the Layer 2 design has
been written. It is recorded here so that the Layer 1 work has an
explicit pointer to the deferred work and so that the trace matrix
links the two layers.
<<<
RELATIONS: FUNC-FACADE-001, FUNC-FACADE-004

[/SECTION]
